  "$comment": "THE redirect table. This file is the single source of truth for /t/{code} and /q/{code}. The CloudFront Function, the NFCTags seed, the chip encoding input and the QR artwork sheet are all compiled from it by scripts/build.mjs and are never hand edited. Editing a targetPath here and redeploying is the supported way to repoint a blend without re-encoding a tag, which is the entire reason the redirect exists. targetPath serves the tap and qrTargetPath serves the on-pack QR: they are the same destination page and differ only in the via value the beacon reads after paint. qrUrl is the exact string Trevean encodes into the on-pack artwork. Do not edit dist/ by hand: CI regenerates it and fails on a difference.",
